DATA CAVEATS: W1: the rebuilt parent NAV is rebuilt from the parent's baskets and Eikon prices, not validated against a published NAV before 2019-01-02; manual Eikon exports for delisted stocks are held in W1 (R7); the sessions 2017-10-19 and the GOLDBEES gap use stand-ins; price returns only; the cash file's source before 2026-08-10 is unrecorded (F-AA-D09), which matters most in -liq (100% of the regime holding is cash); BOTH WINDOWS ARE SEEN: T06, T08, T11, T13 ran the original rules on these weeks before the variants were proposed, so any finding is PROVISIONAL at most and there is NO HOLD-OUT. Picking the best of the six rules from these tables is a selection on seen data.
CONVENTIONS: returns in %, differences in pp (percentage points of CAGR; drawdown differences in pp of drawdown, positive = shallower); CAGR = end NAV ^ (252 / (sessions - 1)) - 1; years = (sessions - 1) / 252; max drawdown = min over t of NAV_t / max(NAV_s, s <= t) - 1; Calmar = CAGR / |max drawdown|; volatility = SD of daily returns x sqrt(252); 20.8 bps = 10.4 bps a side on every value traded (0 and 50 as robustness); percentile = (draws worse + 0.5 ties) / draws x 100; p = (1 + draws at least as good) / (draws + 1); MDE = 2.8 x SD of the null's statistic.

